  "in_reply_to_user_id" : 14552559,
  "text" : "@thewolfstar @KatWitchyWoman @lydasSockPuppet @rin_is_done @Hamburgler08 @thefreerifleman @Dj12gauge00 @AgoristRobot @1Marchella @planetaryjim @TheGuvenuh @RwaysResilient @JaquesTowaki1 @iamlibertatem @MrMcFuckyou @LPMisesCaucus @Scary155 @ThomasEWoods @panzersharkcat @BadQuakerBen @LuminousNebulae @mnrothbard @anarcho7 @fare @MaryRuwart @USlawreview @AntonioBuehler @JeremyLyda @Zero_Gov @JayPHailey @jcomeau_ictx @Bill_Martin_III @AnarchoXP @Anarchyball Well, it\u2019s hard to classify them. I consider non-sapient creatures (e.g. fetuses) and things to be property. Kids are sapient creatures, but not yet fully able to consent. I understand why you don\u2019t like the \u201Cproperty\u201D characterization, but I don\u2019t know what else to use.",
